  "full_prompt": "Create an animation explaining the derivative of exponential functions. Start with 2^t as population growth that doubles each day. Show that the derivative of 2^t is proportional to itself: d(2^t)/dt = 2^t · ln(2). Derive this using the exponential property 2^(t+dt) = 2^t · 2^(dt), showing the constant ln(2) emerges as dt → 0. Introduce e as the special base where the proportionality constant is 1, making d(e^t)/dt = e^t. Show how e is defined by this property, similar to how π is defined by circles. Connect to the chain rule: d(e^(c·t))/dt = c·e^(c·t). Finally, explain that any exponential can be written as e^(c·t), where c = ln(a), making the constant c represent the proportionality between the function and its rate of change.",
